      "blue_ringed_octopus_specialty_signal_a": "Blue-ringed octopus specialty: signal aposematic warning rings + deliver tetrodotoxin if attacked. Most predators learn to avoid blue-ringed individuals after one encounter — or don't survive to learn.",
      "blue_ringed_octopuses_can_rapidly_flas": "Blue-ringed octopuses can rapidly flash their iridescent blue rings — completing the full display in <60 ms. This APOSEMATIC signal warns predators of their tetrodotoxin venom.",
      "blue_ringed_octopuses_carry_tetrodotox": "Blue-ringed octopuses carry tetrodotoxin — the same toxin in pufferfish — 1000x more potent than cyanide. The bite is painless but causes paralysis in minutes; there is no antivenom.",
      "blue_ringed_octopuses_produce_tetrodot": "Blue-ringed octopuses produce tetrodotoxin — the same toxin in pufferfish, 1200x more potent than cyanide by mass. The bite is painless but lethal.",
